  <h1>Lesson 47: Deploy Free - Put Your Website LIVE on Internet</h1>
  <p>Free Hosting, Free Domain, Free HTTPS - In 5 Minutes | LearnHTMLCSSJS.com</p>
</header>

<div class="container">
  <div class="tabs">
    <button id="lessonTabBtn" class="tab-btn active" onclick="showLesson()">📖 Lesson</button>
    <button id="testTabBtn" class="tab-btn" onclick="showTest()">📝 Test - 100 Marks</button>
  </div>
  <div id="lockMsg" class="lock-msg">🔒 Test is running! All tabs are locked until you submit the test or time ends.</div>

  <div id="lessonContent">
    <h2>1. What is Deploy?</h2>
    <p><b>Deploy = Put your website on the internet so anyone in the world can open it.</b></p>
    <p>Until now, your website only lives on YOUR computer. Only you can see it. When you deploy, you upload it to a server - A computer that is always ON - And you get a link like <b>https://ali-portfolio.netlify.app</b>. You can send that link to anyone - Client, friend, company. They open it on their phone and see your website.</p>
    <div class="note"><b>Good News:</b> For HTML CSS JS websites, deploy is 100% FREE. No credit card, no payment. Netlify, Vercel, GitHub Pages - All free. You will deploy today in 5 minutes.</div>
    <h2>2. LIVE DEMO - Deploy Checklist - Tick As You Go</h2>
    <p>Follow these steps in real life. Tick each box here to track your progress:</p>
    <div class="demo-card">
      <div class="deploy-wrap">
        <h3 style="text-align:center;margin:0">🚀 Deploy Checklist - <span id="deployPct">0%</span> Done</h3>
        <div class="progress"><div class="progress-bar" id="deployBar"></div></div>
        <div class="deploy-step" id="step1"><div class="deploy-num">1</div><div><b>Save your file as index.html</b><br><span style="font-size:13px;color:#64748b">Your main file MUST be named index.html - Not mywebsite.html</span><br><button class="btn" style="padding:6px 12px;font-size:13px" onclick="toggleStep(1)">Mark Done ✅</button></div></div>
        <div class="deploy-step" id="step2"><div class="deploy-num">2</div><div><b>Put all files in ONE folder</b><br><span style="font-size:13px;color:#64748b">Folder: my-website / index.html + images + style.css</span><br><button class="btn" style="padding:6px 12px;font-size:13px" onclick="toggleStep(2)">Mark Done ✅</button></div></div>
        <div class="deploy-step" id="step3"><div class="deploy-num">3</div><div><b>Go to netlify.com - Sign up free</b><br><span style="font-size:13px;color:#64748b">Use Google / GitHub to sign up - No card needed</span><br><button class="btn" style="padding:6px 12px;font-size:13px" onclick="toggleStep(3)">Mark Done ✅</button></div></div>
        <div class="deploy-step" id="step4"><div class="deploy-num">4</div><div><b>Drag & Drop your folder</b><br><span style="font-size:13px;color:#64748b">Netlify dashboard → Drag folder → Wait 30 seconds</span><br><button class="btn" style="padding:6px 12px;font-size:13px" onclick="toggleStep(4)">Mark Done ✅</button></div></div>
        <div class="deploy-step" id="step5"><div class="deploy-num">5</div><div><b>Copy your live link + Test on phone</b><br><span style="font-size:13px;color:#64748b">Open link on mobile, check all buttons, share with friends!</span><br><button class="btn" style="padding:6px 12px;font-size:13px" onclick="toggleStep(5)">Mark Done ✅</button></div></div>
        <p id="deployMsg" style="text-align:center;font-weight:bold;color:#16a34a"></p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <h2>3. 3 Free Ways to Deploy - Which One?</h2>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Platform</th><th>How?</th><th>Best For</th></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Netlify Drop</b> ⭐ Easiest</td><td>Go to app.netlify.com/drop - Drag folder - Done</td><td>Beginners - No account setup, 30 seconds</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Vercel</b></td><td>Go to vercel.com - Import from GitHub or drag</td><td>Fast, professional - Many companies use it</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>GitHub Pages</b></td><td>Push code to GitHub → Settings → Pages → Deploy</td><td>Learn Git + Show code to companies</td></tr>
    </table>
    <div class="note"><b>Start with Netlify Drop.</b> No Git, no command, no setup. Just drag your folder. When you learn Git, move to GitHub Pages + Vercel. All 3 give free HTTPS - Your link starts with https://</div>
    <h2>4. Step by Step - Netlify Drop (Easiest)</h2>
    <p>1. Open your computer - Make a folder named <code>my-website</code><br>2. Inside folder, save your website as <code>index.html</code> - If you have images, put them in same folder<br>3. Open browser - Go to <b>app.netlify.com/drop</b><br>4. Drag your <code>my-website</code> folder onto the page - Drop it<br>5. Wait 30 seconds - Netlify gives you a link like <code>https://amazing-site-123.netlify.app</code><br>6. Click link - Your website is LIVE! Open on phone to test<br>7. Change name - Site settings → Change site name → <code>ali-portfolio</code> → New link: <code>https://ali-portfolio.netlify.app</code></p>
    <h2>5. Folder Structure - Must Be Correct</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">✅ CORRECT - index.html at top, images in same folder</span><br>
<span class="text">my-website /</span><br>
<span class="text">├── index.html &lt;!-- Main file - MUST be this name --&gt;</span><br>
<span class="text">├── style.css &lt;!-- If you have separate CSS --&gt;</span><br>
<span class="text">├── script.js &lt;!-- If you have separate JS --&gt;</span><br>
<span class="text">└── biryani.jpg &lt;!-- Images in same folder --&gt;</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">❌ WRONG - index.html inside another folder</span><br>
<span class="text">my-website /</span><br>
<span class="text">└── my-website /</span><br>
<span class="text">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;└── index.html &lt;!-- Netlify cannot find it - Shows blank --&gt;</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">❌ WRONG - Main file named wrong</span><br>
<span class="text">my-website /</span><br>
<span class="text">└── mywebsite.html &lt;!-- Must be index.html, not any other name --&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>6. After Deploy - Update Your Website</h2>
    <p>Website is not one-time. You will update it many times - New project, new price, fix mistake.</p>
    <p><b>Netlify Drop:</b> Fix file on computer → Drag folder again → Same link updates in 30 seconds.<br><b>GitHub Pages:</b> Fix file → Push to GitHub → Site updates automatically in 1 minute.<br><b>Tip:</b> Always test on phone after update. 80% of your visitors are on phone.</p>
    <h2>7. Domain - Free vs Paid</h2>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Type</th><th>Example</th><th>Price</th><th>When?</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Free Subdomain</td><td>ali-portfolio.netlify.app</td><td>Free</td><td>Start - Portfolio, practice, first clients</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Custom Domain</td><td>aliwebstudio.com</td><td>Rs. 2,000-3,000 / year</td><td>When you get paying clients - Looks professional</td></tr>
    </table>
    <p>Buy custom domain later from Namecheap / GoDaddy. Connect to Netlify in 10 minutes - Netlify → Domain settings → Add custom domain. For now, free link is perfect.</p>
    <h2>8. Homework - Deploy 2 Websites TODAY</h2>
    <p>Do not just read. Deploy now:</p>
    <p>1. <b>Your Portfolio (Lesson 42)</b> - Deploy on Netlify - Link like ali-portfolio.netlify.app - Send to 5 friends<br>2. <b>Your Final Project (Lesson 45)</b> - Deploy second site - Send to 1 shop owner - Ask "Would you pay for this?"<br>3. Add both links to your WhatsApp bio + Facebook bio - Now anyone can see your work</p>
    <div class="box"><b>Remember:</b> Deploy = Upload to server, get live link | Main file MUST be index.html | One folder - index.html + images + CSS + JS together | Netlify Drop = Drag folder, 30 seconds, free | After update, drag again | Free link = name.netlify.app | Custom domain later - Rs. 2,000/year | Always test on phone after deploy</div>
    <p><b>Next Step:</b> <a href="/lesson48">Lesson 48 - Freelancing Guide</a> - How to get your first client, price your work, and earn money.</p>
    <a id="playgroundLink" class="btn" href="/playground">▶ Try it Yourself - Playground</a><br><br>
